<title>FRANCE: Santer sees accord on stability pact at EU summit.</title>
<headline>Santer sees accord on stability pact at EU summit.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer said on Wednesday he expected the EU summit in Amsterdam next week to agree on the budget stability pact linked to economic and monetary Union.</p>
<p>&quot;From what I know as a result of the meeting with (Dutch Prime Minister) Wim Kok and (French Prime Minister Mr (Lionel) Jospin...it would seem based on these discussions we can succeed in Amsterdam,&quot; he told a news conference in Strasbourg.  </p>
<p>Kok met both Jospin and French President Jacques Chirac in Paris on Tuesday to discuss the turmoil caused by France's announcement on Monday that it wanted more time to study the pact. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
